WEBVTT

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:08.620
Hi, my name is Roger. I'm a senior software engineer, and I started my career in 2001.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:19.620
So yes, I have a lot of experience behind me. I've worked with many kinds of companies and many kinds of industries.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:28.620
I've developed software for many kinds of architectures and server environments.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:35.620
But I'll focus on my latest projects, or this would be a half-hour video.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:49.620
I can talk a little about a set of microservices: 25 microservices in a fully scalable architecture,

00:00:49.620 --> 00:01:03.620
built to replace legacy systems. Each microservice replaced, one by one, an operation of the legacy monolith.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:10.620
It was great. It was a fully agile development environment,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:25.620
so we could validate step by step, in real time. Every step taught us something about reading and writing documentation.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:40.620
I was the main person responsible for understanding the legacy system and designing the documentation and the architecture of the new system: how one would replace the other.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:50.620
I was the point of contact, working remotely inside the client.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:02:14.620
I followed up on every situation personally, and we had a really good set of metrics and observability, so we could prove the replacement was a full success, 100% okay.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:18.620
So we could release the new software.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:39.620
I was also the main person responsible for onboarding and mentoring, from interns and junior developers to senior developers: setting up how the team works and how to collaborate with it.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:54.620
I've always been a tech lead, even at the beginning of my career. It's something I carry with a lot of pride, and I've received many compliments and thanks for it.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:58.500
Hope we can talk again. Thank you so much.
